-- title:
--   Kernel-ideal dictionary at ℓ for Hom(W,X₀)
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field and $X_0$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Assume given an injective ring homomorphism $\theta$ from [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring κ X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) — the subring of additive endomorphisms of the $\kappa$-points of $X_0$ generated by the rational self-maps, i.e. by those additive maps that are zero or given outside a finite set of $x$-coordinates by ratios of bivariate polynomials over $\kappa$ — into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, whose range is exactly $\Lambda$. Let $W$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ admitting a nonzero element of $H:=$ [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet κ W X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) (the analogous set of rationally represented additive maps on $\kappa$-points from $W$ to $X_0$), and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\neq 0$ in $\kappa$. Then two assertions hold. First, for every additive subgroup $U$ of the $\kappa$-points of $W$ all of whose elements are killed by $\ell$: the set of points $P$ with $\ell P=0$ annihilated by every $\rho\in H$ whose kernel contains $U$ is exactly $U$, and the relative index of the subgroup generated by $\{\rho\in H: U\le\ker\rho\}$ inside the subgroup generated by $H$ equals $(\#U)^2$. Second, for every additive subgroup $M$ of the additive maps from the $\kappa$-points of $W$ to those of $X_0$ with $M\subseteq H$, with $\ell\rho\in M$ for all $\rho\in H$, and with $\alpha\circ\rho\in M$ for all $\rho\in M$ and all rational self-maps $\alpha$ of $X_0$: any $\rho\in H$ vanishing at every $\ell$-torsion point killed by all members of $M$ lies in $M$.
--
--   This is Waterhouse's kernel-ideal calculus at a prime $\ell$ invertible in $\kappa$, transposed from $\mathrm{End}(X_0)$ to the module $\mathrm{Hom}(W,X_0)$ and supplemented by the index formula $[H:H(U)]=\#U^2$; the hypotheses on $\theta$ and $\Lambda$ identify the rational endomorphism ring of $X_0$ with a quaternion order, hence of $\mathbb{Z}$-rank $4$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where subgroups of $\mathrm{Hom}(W,X_0)$ stable under the endomorphism ring are matched with finite subgroups of $W$ and with Hecke data at $\ell$.
-- source:
